1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,640
Last time, we learnt that a freely suspended magnet comes to rest

2
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:07,250
in the North-South direction, every time.

3
00:00:07,730 --> 00:00:10,320
That is because Earth behaves like a magnet.

4
00:00:11,935 --> 00:00:14,625
A little sea turtle is hiding in this video.

5
00:00:14,865 --> 00:00:16,105
Can you spot it?

6
00:00:16,229 --> 00:00:17,659
Turtles pop up to breathe.

7
00:00:17,859 --> 00:00:19,009
Watch the water!

8
00:00:19,135 --> 00:00:20,975
Lock in first with your fingers.

9
00:00:21,245 --> 00:00:23,075
One finger for every point.

10
00:00:23,662 --> 00:00:24,832
Today you'll learn:

11
00:00:25,028 --> 00:00:26,348
How a compass works.

12
00:00:26,547 --> 00:00:28,127
A magnet near a compass.

13
00:00:28,326 --> 00:00:29,626
Telling the direction.

14
00:00:31,229 --> 00:00:32,109
Round one.

15
00:00:32,429 --> 00:00:35,859
Basil brings his bar magnet close to Momo's compass.

16
00:00:36,139 --> 00:00:37,199
What happens?

17
00:00:37,459 --> 00:00:38,989
One, nothing happens.

18
00:00:39,249 --> 00:00:40,739
Two, the needle turns.

19
00:00:41,009 --> 00:00:44,079
Three, the needle spins round and round, forever.

20
00:00:44,369 --> 00:00:45,719
Show me your fingers.

21
00:00:51,190 --> 00:00:52,170
Locked in!

22
00:00:52,298 --> 00:00:52,888
One.

23
00:00:53,278 --> 00:00:56,198
A compass needle always points North and South.

24
00:00:56,358 --> 00:00:58,138
Nothing can change that.

25
00:00:58,187 --> 00:00:58,967
Two!

26
00:00:59,047 --> 00:01:01,357
I think the needle is a tiny magnet.

27
00:01:01,437 --> 00:01:04,367
Then Basil's magnet can attract it, or repel it.

28
00:01:04,422 --> 00:01:05,042
Two!

29
00:01:05,212 --> 00:01:07,652
My magnet pulls and pushes other magnets.

30
00:01:07,692 --> 00:01:08,992
The needle will turn!

31
00:01:09,268 --> 00:01:10,678
Be the compass needle!

32
00:01:10,958 --> 00:01:11,938
Shrink down.

33
00:01:12,218 --> 00:01:13,148
Quietly.

34
00:01:15,434 --> 00:01:19,424
You are the needle inside a compass, balanced on a tiny pin.

35
00:01:20,194 --> 00:01:21,674
You can turn freely.

36
00:01:22,182 --> 00:01:24,272
You swing, and slow, and stop.

37
00:01:25,052 --> 00:01:27,052
Your red end points to the North.

38
00:01:27,561 --> 00:01:29,371
Here comes a bar magnet!

39
00:01:30,141 --> 00:01:31,911
Your red end is pushed away.

40
00:01:32,671 --> 00:01:36,401
The magnet turns round, and now your red end is pulled in.

41
00:01:36,923 --> 00:01:38,443
The magnet goes away.

42
00:01:39,243 --> 00:01:41,663
You swing back to the North-South direction.

43
00:01:43,322 --> 00:01:46,652
The answer is two: the needle turns towards or away from the

44
00:01:46,672 --> 00:01:47,462
magnet!

45
00:01:47,722 --> 00:01:49,302
Did you show two fingers?

46
00:01:49,572 --> 00:01:50,940
Put one finger up!

47
00:01:50,960 --> 00:01:54,280
The needle is the small magnet inside a compass, such as this

48
00:01:54,300 --> 00:01:55,440
thin red one.

49
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:58,670
My magnet attracted one end, and repelled the other!

50
00:01:59,244 --> 00:01:59,944
Easy!

51
00:02:00,084 --> 00:02:01,824
The needle points to the letter N.

52
00:02:02,014 --> 00:02:05,144
If I turn the compass round, the needle turns round with it!

53
00:02:05,791 --> 00:02:06,941
Look closer.

54
00:02:07,521 --> 00:02:08,961
Turn the compass round.

55
00:02:09,521 --> 00:02:12,257
The letters turn, but the needle does not!

56
00:02:12,277 --> 00:02:15,837
So turn the compass until the N sits under the needle's red

57
00:02:15,857 --> 00:02:16,487
end.

58
00:02:17,067 --> 00:02:18,914
Now you know which way is North!

59
00:02:18,934 --> 00:02:22,304
A compass is a tool that helps us find the direction, such

60
00:02:22,324 --> 00:02:24,034
as my hiking compass!

61
00:02:27,332 --> 00:02:28,632
Say it with me!

62
00:02:29,343 --> 00:02:31,883
A compass can help us to find the direction.

63
00:02:32,383 --> 00:02:36,253
When the needle inside the compass stops moving, it always points in

64
00:02:36,273 --> 00:02:38,353
the North-South direction of the Earth.

65
00:02:41,827 --> 00:02:42,737
Showdown!

66
00:02:43,037 --> 00:02:44,167
Double points.

67
00:02:44,437 --> 00:02:47,187
Momo's compass checklist has one mistake.

68
00:02:47,457 --> 00:02:49,247
Line one, two, or three?

69
00:02:49,537 --> 00:02:51,007
Show me with your fingers.

70
00:02:51,069 --> 00:02:54,419
One: hold the compass flat, so the needle can turn freely.

71
00:02:54,439 --> 00:02:56,969
Two: wait until the needle stops moving.

72
00:02:57,049 --> 00:03:00,949
Three: keep Basil's magnet right next to the compass, to help it.

73
00:03:06,556 --> 00:03:07,536
Locked in!

74
00:03:07,664 --> 00:03:08,404
Three!

75
00:03:08,494 --> 00:03:10,784
My magnet attracts and repels the needle.

76
00:03:10,984 --> 00:03:13,764
Then the needle cannot show the North-South direction!

77
00:03:14,638 --> 00:03:15,728
Three fingers?

78
00:03:15,968 --> 00:03:17,868
Put up two more on your score hand!

79
00:03:18,138 --> 00:03:20,958
Keep magnets and phones away from your compass.

80
00:03:21,173 --> 00:03:23,983
But what if it is night, and we cannot see the Sun?

81
00:03:24,223 --> 00:03:25,993
Will a compass still work?

82
00:03:26,641 --> 00:03:27,791
Look closer.

83
00:03:28,381 --> 00:03:31,261
At night, a ship sails in the Singapore Strait.

84
00:03:31,831 --> 00:03:33,487
Clouds hide the stars.

85
00:03:33,507 --> 00:03:36,987
But the needle in the ship's compass still comes to rest in

86
00:03:37,007 --> 00:03:38,480
the North-South direction.

87
00:03:38,500 --> 00:03:42,070
Far away in the United States, a hiker is lost in thick

88
00:03:42,090 --> 00:03:42,820
fog.

89
00:03:43,390 --> 00:03:45,093
Her compass works there too!

90
00:03:45,113 --> 00:03:49,013
Tell the direction means find out which way is North, South, East

91
00:03:49,033 --> 00:03:51,423
or West, such as on a ship at night!

92
00:03:54,720 --> 00:03:55,940
Say it with me!

93
00:03:56,651 --> 00:04:00,751
Hence, a freely suspended magnet can be used to tell the direction.

94
00:04:03,507 --> 00:04:04,612
Say it with us!

95
00:04:05,272 --> 00:04:06,500
Hang it freely?

96
00:04:06,852 --> 00:04:07,891
North-South!

97
00:04:11,672 --> 00:04:12,980
A compass needle?

98
00:04:13,252 --> 00:04:14,499
A small magnet!

99
00:04:18,072 --> 00:04:19,273
Why North-South?

100
00:04:19,652 --> 00:04:21,402
Earth behaves like a magnet!

101
00:04:25,227 --> 00:04:26,687
Show me your score hand!

102
00:04:26,967 --> 00:04:28,417
Two fingers or more?

103
00:04:28,707 --> 00:04:30,067
You beat the Buddies.

104
00:04:30,357 --> 00:04:31,427
Three fingers?

105
00:04:31,707 --> 00:04:32,707
High five!

106
00:04:32,910 --> 00:04:34,530
Did you spot the sea turtle?

107
00:04:34,820 --> 00:04:37,680
It was in the seagrass, at the end of the boardwalk!

108
00:04:37,801 --> 00:04:39,391
Here is a fun fact!

109
00:04:39,551 --> 00:04:42,001
Sea turtles can feel the Earth's magnet.

110
00:04:42,231 --> 00:04:45,191
It helps them find their way across the ocean, back to the

111
00:04:45,211 --> 00:04:46,661
beach where they hatched!

112
00:04:46,782 --> 00:04:48,062
Tell someone at home!

113
00:04:49,001 --> 00:04:53,441
Next time: Pip strokes an iron nail with Basil's magnet, again and

114
00:04:53,461 --> 00:04:55,371
again, always the same way.

115
00:04:55,641 --> 00:04:58,651
Then he holds the nail near some steel paper clips.

116
00:04:58,931 --> 00:04:59,981
What happens?

117
00:05:00,251 --> 00:05:01,771
One, nothing happens.

118
00:05:02,051 --> 00:05:04,121
Two, the nail attracts the clips.

119
00:05:04,381 --> 00:05:05,711
Lock in your answer!

120
00:05:05,983 --> 00:05:08,183
Let's read today's key words together!

121
00:05:08,473 --> 00:05:09,233
Ready?

122
00:05:09,520 --> 00:05:10,310
Needle.

123
00:05:11,612 --> 00:05:12,502
Compass.

124
00:05:13,835 --> 00:05:15,045
Tell the direction.

125
00:05:16,683 --> 00:05:17,623
Well done!

126
00:05:18,605 --> 00:05:19,706
Say it with us!

127
00:05:20,506 --> 00:05:21,256
Ready?

128
00:05:21,380 --> 00:05:22,040
One!

129
00:05:22,380 --> 00:05:23,080
two!

130
00:05:23,385 --> 00:05:24,560
Now you know!
